  "findings": [
    "The fixed strictly positive residual damping, local Drude response, permeability1 and explicit exclusion of superconductivity determine unscreened static magnetic fields. The TE zero Matsubara amplitude vanishes, while TM tends1.",
    "The source uses the plasma static boundary prescription only at the zero Matsubara term. This is a completed, calibration-equivalent physical approximation: the isolated point has measure zero in the T0 integral.",
    "The y=2aq and u=xi/q Jacobians give pressure prefactors -1/(32*pi^2*a^4) at T0 and -T/(8*pi*a^3) for the primed finite-T sum. Both source and oracle implement those correctly.",
    "The independent reference differentiates free energy with a five-point separation derivative and evaluates the Drude surface-impedance limit at small positive xi. Its energy prefactors, half weight and pressure sign are consistent.",
    "Global equilibrium and explicit residual damping avoid an ambiguity about order of temperature and material-relaxation limits. The ideal response is part of the apparatus; the task does not assert an experimental resolution of the Drude-plasma controversy."
  ],
  "source": "https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0212125",
